**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** What a fit run promotes to the library, as pure values: a fitted material is its opened version's entry holding the fitted crystal, and a fitted black-box object is a custom-Mueller polarizer preset of its fitted matrix (001 §I 'Promote to library mints the material's next version in the database, with provenance "fitted in kit K, study S, run R"'; 001 §L 'material or black-box object → Promote to library'; 001 §I table 'Sample as black-box Mueller matrix: 16 parameters (or 15 + scale) at reference orientation'; the S11.5 brief). A black-box object's library form is the polarizer preset, because the preset is the one library kind that holds a fixed Mueller matrix (`ElementId.fs:PolarizerBehavior`'s `ConstantMueller`, `ElementId.fs:PolarizerCategory`'s `CustomMueller`, 'a custom Mueller stack'), while an item-model form holds no values (step 208) and a stack sample holds layers. Its entry takes the item's GUID, so promoting the same item again finds the entry and mints its next version (step 408). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5, and every case name has two words. In `StudyPublishing.fs`, after `calibratedItemsWith` (step 406): (1) `type ItemId with member this.toLibraryEntryId : LibraryEntryId` (the GUID kept, as `MaterialId.toLibraryEntryId` keeps it, step 24) and `member this.toElementValueId : ElementValueId` (the GUID's canonical text, as `SampleId.toElementValueId` writes it); `type ItemLabel with member this.entryName : EntryName`, the label's text. No conversion goes the other way (ELEV006). (2) `type FitRun with member this.provenanceIn (kit : KitId) : EntryProvenance`: `FitProvenance { kit = kit; studyStem = this.study.fileStem; fitRunStem = this.name.fileStem }` (steps 358, 383, 405). (3) `PromotionSubject` = `MaterialPromotion of MaterialVersionId` (an opened material version, step 361) | `BlackBoxPromotion of ItemId` (a black-box item): what `PromoteToLibrary` names (001 §P). It is derived, never stored, so it carries no tag. (4) `PublishError` (step 406) gains `UnfittedPromotionErr of reason : string` (`the fit run fitted none of its values: <reason>`), `ScopedPromotionErr of reason : string` (`the fit gives it no single value: <reason>`, a value fitted per session block or per run), `NotBlackBoxErr of reason : string` (`the item is not a black-box Mueller matrix: <reason>`), `PromotionStudyErr of error : StudyError` (`the study refused the promoted value: <the error's describe>`) and `PromotionEvaluationErr of error : ItemEvaluationError` (`the fitted matrix could not be evaluated: <the error's describe>`, step 247). (5) `type Study with member this.promotedMaterialWith (run : FitRun) (version : MaterialVersionId) (entry : MaterialEntry) : Result<MaterialEntry, PublishError>`, over the entry the caller resolved for `version`: `ForeignFitRunErr` as in step 406; the opened copy is the one of `this.materials` of that version (else `UnfittedPromotionErr` naming it); the run's entries of `MaterialParameterRef (version, name)` (step 358) are its fitted components, one owned by anything but `MaterialOwner version` answering `ScopedPromotionErr` naming the component, and none answering `UnfittedPromotionErr` naming the material and the run. Each component of the copy is set through `withParameterState` (step 361, its error `PromotionStudyErr`) to `KnownParameter` of its fitted value when the run fitted it, and otherwise to the state `run.parameters` (step 383) records for it, the state the fit read. The answer is `{ entry with physics = CrystalParameterPhysics <that copy's currentCrystal> }` (steps 355, 361): every other field of the entry is kept, its id is the material's, and so the library mints that material's next version (step 408). (6) `type FitRun with member this.promotedBlackBoxWith (item : Item) (choice : ItemModelChoice) : Result<PolarizerPreset, PublishError>`: `choice` a `LibraryModelChoice` whose form is `OpticalElementModel (BlackBoxMuellerModel normalisation)` (steps 208, 216), else `NotBlackBoxErr` naming the item's label; the run's entries of `ItemParameterRef (item.id, name)` are its fitted elements, one owned by anything but `ItemOwner item.id` answering `ScopedPromotionErr` and none answering `UnfittedPromotionErr`. Its values are `ParameterValues.ofParameters` (step 245) of the item's parameters, each fitted one as `KnownParameter` of its fitted value and each other in the state `run.parameters` records for it. Its matrix is the bound form `BoundOpticalForm (BlackBoxMuellerModel normalisation, values)` (`BoundOpticalElement.ofOpticalForm`, step 248) evaluated by `muellerAt` at rotation zero, normal incidence and the transmitted branch, its reference orientation, as `realizabilityWith` evaluates a black box (step 402), at the 600 nm `SourcePreset.operatingWaveLengthOf` answers without a source (step 367), which a black-box form does not read (step 248); an evaluation error answers `PromotionEvaluationErr`. The answer is `{ id = item.id.toElementValueId; name = item.label.entryName; behavior = ConstantMueller [ { matrix = <the matrix>; offset = Angle 0.0 } ]; category = CustomMueller; protection = UserManaged }` (`ElementId.fs:PolarizerPreset`, `ElementId.fs:MuellerComponent`): one component at reference orientation, turned at run time as any element is (001 §I 'rotation as R(−φ) M R(φ)'). (7) `type FitRun with member this.promotionSubjectsWith (study : Study) (items : Item list) (choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option) : PromotionSubject list`: the study's opened materials, in study order, of which the run has a `MaterialParameterRef` entry, each as `MaterialPromotion`, then the items of `items`, in order, whose `choiceOf` answers a black-box `LibraryModelChoice` and of which the run has an `ItemParameterRef` entry, each as `BlackBoxPromotion`; the Publish step lists them (step 418). Nothing is written. No other type or member is added. Tests, in `StudyPublishingTests` (step 406). `a promoted material is its opened version's entry with the crystal its fit run produced`: over a test-local absorbing crystal entry of fifteen distinct literal values (as `StudyMaterialTests` builds its probe, step 361) opened by the study, with `n1` and `e11` unknown, and a run of the study fitting `n1` at 1.7 and `e11` at 0.02 (`MaterialOwner`) whose `parameters` record every other component at the probe's value: `promotedMaterialWith` answers the entry under `CrystalParameterPhysics` whose generated axes read 1.7 for `n1`, 0.02 for `e11` and the probe's value for every other component, its id and name unchanged. `a material component fitted per run, or a material the study did not open or the run did not fit, is not promoted`: `n1` owned by an `ExperimentOwner` answers `ScopedPromotionErr` naming `n1`; a version the study did not open, and a run with no entry of the material, each answer `UnfittedPromotionErr`. `a promoted black box is a custom-Mueller polarizer preset of its fitted matrix under the item's GUID and label`: QZ over the built-in black-box model (`ItemModelIds.blackBoxMuellerModelId`, sixteen elements at the identity, step 208), with `m00` fitted at 0.9 and `m01` at 0.25 (`ItemOwner`), answers the preset whose id is QZ's GUID text, named `QZ`, `CustomMueller` and `UserManaged`, with one `ConstantMueller` component at offset zero whose matrix holds 0.9 at (0, 0), 0.25 at (0, 1) and the identity elsewhere, within 1e-15; CPL1 over the circular-polarizer model answers `NotBlackBoxErr` naming `CPL1`; and QZ's `m01` owned by an `ExperimentOwner` answers `ScopedPromotionErr`. `a fit run's provenance names its kit, its study's file and its own file`: `provenanceIn` of a test-local `KitId` is `FitProvenance { kit = <it>; studyStem = FileStem "QZ-LR"; fitRunStem = FileStem "QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z" }`. `a fit run offers each opened material and black box it fitted for promotion`: over CPL1, QZ and the opened material, `promotionSubjectsWith` of a run fitting `n1`, CPL1's `c2.retardance` and QZ's `m00` answers `MaterialPromotion` of the opened version, then `BlackBoxPromotion` of QZ; of a run fitting CPL1 alone, `[]`. `every publish error renders its condition and its payload` covers the five new cases. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the promoted values land, `Study.promotedMaterialWith` MUST answer the opened version's entry holding the crystal its fit run produced, `FitRun.promotedBlackBoxWith` MUST answer a custom-Mueller polarizer preset of the item's fitted matrix under its GUID and label, `FitRun.provenanceIn` MUST answer the fitted provenance and `promotionSubjectsWith` MUST list what the run can promote, values fitted per session or run refused; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a promoted material is its opened version's entry with the crystal its fit run produced`, `a material component fitted per run, or a material the study did not open or the run did not fit, is not promoted`, `a promoted black box is a custom-Mueller polarizer preset of its fitted matrix under the item's GUID and label`, `a fit run's provenance names its kit, its study's file and its own file` and `a fit run offers each opened material and black box it fitted for promotion`, the count rising by 5, and the widened `every publish error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.
